{"schemaVersion":1,"systemCode":"DIN:yid-Hebr:Latn:31636-2018","dependencies":[],"metadata":{"authority_id":"din","id":"31636-2018","language":"iso-639-2:yid","source_script":"Hebr","destination_script":"Latn","name":"DIN 31636:2018-10 Information und Dokumentation - Umschrift des hebraeischen Alphabets (jiddische Spalte)","url":"https://www.din.de","creation_date":"2018","confirmation_date":"2018-10","description":"Information and documentation -- Romanization of the Hebrew alphabet, Yiddish\n    column. 2018-10 edition, replacing DIN 31636:2011-01. This map implements the\n    Yiddish column of Table 1 with the Yiddish vowel table (Table 4) and the Yiddish\n    notes (section 9) of the norm. The Hebrew column is a separate map.","notes":["Consonants (Table 1, Yiddish column): alef is rendered with the right half-ring U+02BE or as the vowel a/o via the vowel spellings; bet with dagesh b, bet v; gimel g; dalet d; he h; vav v with dot below (U+1E7F); double vav (U+05F0) is annotated als Konsonant and shares the row's consonantal rendering; zayin z; het h with dot below (U+1E25); tet t with dot below (U+1E6D); yod y; double yod (U+05F2) is annotated als Konsonant when consonantal, and as a vowel per Table 4 (ay or ey); kaf with dagesh k, khaf kh; lamed l; mem m; nun n; samekh s; ayin e; pe p, fe f; tsadi ts; kof k with dot below (k + U+0323); resh r; shin sh, sin s with acute (U+015B); tav s with grave (U+0073+0300) per section 9(c) - the voiceless-s pronunciation of tav.","Vowels (Table 4): alef with patach (U+FB2A? no - U+05D0+05B7) a; alef with qamats (U+05D0+05B8) a or o - this map renders a, the o-reading is a pronunciation-side determination; ayin e; vav or alef-vav u or o - this map renders u, the norm's own section 9(a) examples use the o-reading (moyre, koyles); vav-yod (U+05F1) or alef-vav-yod oy; yod or alef-yod i; yod-yod (U+05F2) or alef-yod-yod ay or ey, je nach Aussprache - this map renders ay and documents ey as the alternative reading of the same spelling.","Section 9(a): Hebrew words occurring in a Yiddish context are verified for Yiddish pronunciation in Weinreich and then transliterated with Table 1 (Yiddish) and Table 4; Hebrew proper names in a Yiddish context follow the Yiddish pronunciation. The distinction between tav/tet, kof/khaf and khaf/het is made with the underdots, and word-final he is rendered h.","Section 9(c): tav pronounced as voiceless s is rendered with the grave (s + U+0300), e.g. bes (beyt-yod-tav).","Section 9(d): vowels not written in Old Yiddish may optionally be marked with a stroke above the vowel; this map does not add such marks.","Words whose vowels are not written in the spelling (loshn-koydesh items such as the norm's own mehaber/moyre examples) are an underspecified skeleton: the unwritten vowels are resolved by a vocalization model, after which this map applies (composition, not duplication).","Capitalization and hyphenation follow the rules given for Hebrew (rule 8i/b); this map outputs lower case."]},"stages":[{"kind":"stage","name":"main","rules":[{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"אַ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"a"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"אָ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"a"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"אױ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"oy"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"או"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"u"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"אי"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"i"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"אײ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"ay"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ױ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"oy"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ײ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"ay"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"שׂ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"ś"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"שׁ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"sh"}},{"kind":"parallel","rules":[{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"stri